    /// <summary>
    /// Traversal diagnostics plus raid-local learned traversal for Vault/Climb/Jump and grounded
    /// WalkThrough. V1.3.25 promotes player-authored Vault/Climb to EFT's native movement-state
    /// executor using captured native parameters. R8/R8.1 add an adaptive-traversal foundation: unified
    /// anti-snap ownership through Egress/Verify, semantic Jump egress samples, truthful completion
    /// outcomes, automatic diagnostics, and a separate per-map experience database. R8.2 makes
    /// WalkThrough topology PIT-private, adds persistence sanitization/Kind Lock, and protects followers
    /// from out-of-world falls. R8.4 adds platform-landing egress, monotonic WalkThrough arc progress,
    /// partial-native crossing classification, and precision/clearance-aware WalkThrough steering.
    /// R8.5 rejects pathological ordinary Follow detours. R8.6 freezes each follower's oriented
    /// traversal mission, replays post-Jump/Climb egress in 3-D, validates persisted settled anchors,
    /// and reserves Teleport for verified physical hard-stuck recovery. R8.7 extends Jump/Climb into
    /// full Off-NavMesh bridges, makes WalkThrough directional and speed-governed, and migrates adaptive
    /// learning to PolicyVersion 5 with one-time SanitizerRevision 5 cleanup. R8.8 promotes the player's
    /// ordered breadcrumb + traversal history into a follower Route Mission, turns alignment/support checks
    /// into active correction instead of refusal gates, caches pathological Follow rejects, uses a direct
    /// WalkThrough corridor driver, makes native Vault/Climb single-shot, and performs a full movement-authority
    /// reset before every automatic recovery teleport. R8.9 suppresses unnecessary WalkThrough learning when a
    /// cheap nearby NavMesh bypass exists, separates Route Mission approach from exact traversal commitment,
    /// advances a per-follower route floor after manual/recovery teleport so stale queue destinations cannot
    /// re-arm, forces WalkThrough through the direct corridor executor, verifies post-release body integrity,
    /// coalesces longer WalkThrough spans, and captures RampApproach/DropDown semantics for Jump. R8.12 adds
    /// a two-phase ExitAuthority rebase + controlled Follow handoff, PolicyVersion 6 reward semantics,
    /// progress-leased WalkThrough drive, strong quarantine invalidation, and SanitizerRevision 6 toxic-edge
    /// cleanup. R8.12.2 moves TraversalLinks to schema 9 with per-demonstration revisions, aligned semantic
    /// egress evidence, authored Jump/Climb tail replay, bounded island recovery, credible WalkThrough terminal
    /// connectors, and bounded native-entry fallback while preserving stable ExperienceKey learning history.
    /// CompileFix9 advances adaptive learning to PolicyVersion 7 / SanitizerRevision 10, requires
    /// sustained physical Follow acknowledgement before traversal success, suppresses Route Mission
    /// legacy-chain resurrection, and rehabilitates Jump links poisoned by controller-only timeouts.
    /// CompileFix10 advances to PolicyVersion 8 / SanitizerRevision 11, separates physical crossing
    /// reward from five-second end-to-end Follow recovery, learns Native-vs-Assisted executor preference,
    /// and suppresses WalkThrough mover-corner churn while the authored corridor is still progressing.
    /// CompileFix11 keeps PolicyVersion 8 / SanitizerRevision 12 and adds the collision-active SharpTurn
    /// TurnGate, Route-Mission exit handoff, truthful Native/Assisted E2E credit, and FollowAction NRE
    /// containment. CompileFix12 advances SanitizerRevision to 13: rough-ground micro-airborne samples no
    /// longer split a WalkThrough demonstration, player-proven off-NavMesh exits can complete crossing and
    /// ExitAuthority without deadlocking, deferred route recovery is debounced/terminal, and contaminated
    /// WalkThrough execution penalties are rehabilitated without deleting authored geometry.
    /// CompileFix17 raises SanitizerRevision 17 and repairs traversal geometry/executor learning semantics,
    /// reconnects adjacent Route-Mission WalkThrough fragments into one bounded execution corridor,
    /// adds collision-active StepAssist plus same-apex TurnGate retry suppression, and makes terminal
    /// traversal failure release/quarantine the owning Route Mission immediately. CompileFix18 keeps the
    /// persisted PolicyVersion/SanitizerRevision stable while separating Route-Mission lifetime from one
    /// traversal commitment, abandoning stale unreachable chain steps when ordinary Follow is reachable,
    /// reacquiring near-side Egress mover authority before recovery teleport, and feeding Follow/formation
    /// quality back into adaptive selection and Native-vs-Assisted executor preference. CompileFix19 adds an
    /// empirical Route-Mission approach watchdog, experience-aware suppression of repeatedly failing traversal
    /// executors, adaptive continuous WalkThrough locomotion, and asynchronous traversal diagnostics so JSONL
    /// serialization/flush cannot stall the Unity main thread. CompileFix21 isolates PIT hostile-layer filtering
    /// from EFT boss-follower custom brains, recognizes already-crossed traversal bodies before replay validation,
    /// separates Jump approach distance from authored traversal span, adds short far-side-failure cooldown, and
    /// keeps post-traversal entry quarantine active through the full integrity watch. CompileFix22 makes Jump
    /// direction-sensitive, prevents route-mission rebase from skipping an unconsumed traversal barrier, prefers
    /// Vault/Climb semantic siblings over overlapping Jump edges, and splits Jump entry capture from crossing yaw.
    /// Grenade planning now
    /// validates throw origin and uses a synchronous planning-only runtime gate with per-candidate tracing.
    /// </summary>
